WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
In fact, we operate in a world of biases.

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.020
And here, we will learn little by little, because we will broaden our vision,

3
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:11.660
it's about living with our eyes a bit more open.

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.980
Learning to spot our own patterns.

5
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.100
And I will invite you to observe a pattern.

6
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.500
And if you manage to observe it,

7
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.460
you can...

8
00:00:29.852 --> 00:00:35.332
Most of the time, we use others as

9
00:00:35.332 --> 00:00:38.912
our own rags to clean our own windows.

10
00:00:39.692 --> 00:00:44.812
Have you ever noticed that in your patterns, it

11
00:00:44.812 --> 00:00:45.492
has to be seen,

12
00:00:46.492 --> 00:00:54.012
that we project our satisfaction patterns onto

13
00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:55.112
the outside?

14
00:00:56.144 --> 00:00:57.844
on a subject or on an object.

15
00:00:59.064 --> 00:01:00.804
And then, one day, we are disappointed.

16
00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:03.244
It no longer satisfies me.

17
00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.384
What's important is that at some point,

18
00:01:07.284 --> 00:01:08.504
we blame the other.

19
00:01:10.444 --> 00:01:11.024
We will understand.

20
00:01:11.144 --> 00:01:12.204
Suddenly, I blame the other.

21
00:01:14.264 --> 00:01:15.604
And some people even go further.

22
00:01:15.864 --> 00:01:18.004
When we project too much externally,

23
00:01:18.504 --> 00:01:20.064
we even blame the world.

24
00:01:21.824 --> 00:01:23.284
So it's about observing.

25
00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.317
spotting our own patterns.

26
00:01:27.197 --> 00:01:28.497
One way to achieve this,

27
00:01:29.397 --> 00:01:30.557
is to meditate.

28
00:01:31.117 --> 00:01:33.057
If you want to discover your mind,

29
00:01:34.957 --> 00:01:36.677
You do an exercise, you will see

30
00:01:36.677 --> 00:01:37.617
that after 7 seconds,

31
00:01:38.337 --> 00:01:39.597
thoughts will arise.

32
00:01:40.977 --> 00:01:43.137
And suddenly, you are caught

33
00:01:49.397 --> 00:01:50.617
by a thought.

34
00:01:51.037 --> 00:01:52.097
And meditation,

35
00:01:52.289 --> 00:01:54.349
is about observing that and returning.

36
00:01:56.149 --> 00:02:01.189
And learning to observe something neutral

37
00:02:02.069 --> 00:02:07.129
gradually teaches you to discover your own non-neutral patterns.

38
00:02:08.849 --> 00:02:12.929
So there is a work and an exploration of yourself, if you will.

39
00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:16.629
What do you feel when you see?

40
00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:20.049
It's immediate, it's passive.

41
00:02:20.362 --> 00:02:23.182
You open your eyes, and suddenly the world is there.

42
00:02:24.862 --> 00:02:27.882
And often we think that seeing is believing.

43
00:02:29.142 --> 00:02:31.182
I believe because I have seen.

44
00:02:32.062 --> 00:02:33.982
So we think that vision is truth.

45
00:02:35.442 --> 00:02:37.002
Learning to understand.

46
00:02:38.182 --> 00:02:42.842
What we see is not actually a universal truth.

47
00:02:44.362 --> 00:02:47.042
It’s not a so-called objective reality.

48
00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:51.994
When you work, we have biases.

49
00:02:53.414 --> 00:02:54.874
And that's what you must understand.

50
00:02:55.794 --> 00:02:59.634
Because nature does not take biases into account.

51
00:03:00.674 --> 00:03:03.494
The therapeutic process does not consider that, actually.

52
00:03:04.054 --> 00:03:06.854
These are brakes, false fulcrums.

53
00:03:07.094 --> 00:03:10.674
We create a virtual reality, if you will, that we think is unique.

54
00:03:11.474 --> 00:03:16.434
It’s important to know that your visual cortex uses 30% of the mind.

55
00:03:16.507 --> 00:03:21.667
your brain, 30%, compared to touch

56
00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:25.947
which is 8% and hearing which is only 2-3%.

57
00:03:27.947 --> 00:03:33.527
Every second, your eyes can send about

58
00:03:33.527 --> 00:03:36.227
2 billion bits of information

59
00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:40.547
to your visual cortex, 2 billion.

60
00:03:40.927 --> 00:03:44.507
The rest of your body can only send about a billion.

61
00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:47.319
This means that sight will represent

62
00:03:47.319 --> 00:03:47.979
a third

63
00:03:49.159 --> 00:03:51.079
of your brain volume

64
00:03:51.079 --> 00:03:52.019
a third

65
00:03:53.459 --> 00:03:55.119
and yet it will use

66
00:03:55.119 --> 00:03:56.559
two-thirds of your resources

67
00:03:57.499 --> 00:03:58.999
it's not surprising after all

68
00:03:58.999 --> 00:04:00.699
that it is an illusion if it is important

69
00:04:01.439 --> 00:04:03.619
if I tell you about the Papez circuit

70
00:04:03.619 --> 00:04:05.239
does that ring a bell

71
00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:07.199
all the colliculi and all the nuclei

72
00:04:07.199 --> 00:04:09.179
amygdalae etc. which will integrate

73
00:04:10.519 --> 00:04:11.919
everything you see

74
00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:14.052
influences your emotions.

75
00:04:15.212 --> 00:04:18.032
And your emotions can change what you see.

76
00:04:19.012 --> 00:04:21.892
So this means that sight becomes a mental composition.

77
00:04:23.432 --> 00:04:25.632
We create our own reality.

78
00:04:27.972 --> 00:04:29.372
And on top of that, we believe it.

79
00:04:30.432 --> 00:04:33.212
So this means that this is just one way of forming a reality.

80
00:04:33.992 --> 00:04:37.032
For example, fear, have you ever noticed

81
00:04:37.032 --> 00:04:38.772
how it can distort reality?

82
00:04:39.992 --> 00:04:40.652
I had a child.

83
00:04:40.724 --> 00:04:46.304
who came in, he was traumatized. They had seen a movie.

84
00:04:47.224 --> 00:04:51.064
He associated being

85
00:04:52.084 --> 00:04:57.104
scared with being in danger. And actually, the only thing I did

86
00:04:57.104 --> 00:04:59.804
was dissociate. I said,

87
00:04:59.924 --> 00:05:05.124
you were scared, you were afraid. But

88
00:05:05.124 --> 00:05:06.064
I said, but you are not in danger.

89
00:05:07.444 --> 00:05:08.364
I saw suddenly.

90
00:05:08.797 --> 00:05:12.457
His reality readjusted, you see.

91
00:05:12.977 --> 00:05:16.817
And so once you say this, things fade away, you see.

92
00:05:16.977 --> 00:05:18.997
Because nothing has an existence of its own.

93
00:05:19.337 --> 00:05:20.597
Do you understand that?

94
00:05:20.597 --> 00:05:22.917
Nothing exists by itself.

95
00:05:26.337 --> 00:05:29.137
When we understand this, we have a view that changes.

96
00:05:30.017 --> 00:05:34.577
Because it means we can understand that even the ego does not exist by itself.

97
00:05:34.797 --> 00:05:36.797
It becomes an...

98
00:05:38.069 --> 00:05:43.769
aggregate, showing that everything is interdependent and impermanent.

99
00:05:45.309 --> 00:05:46.889
And impermanence is what

100
00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:52.109
gives energy, because it brings movement. So it gives your

101
00:05:52.109 --> 00:05:55.109
vital energy, actually. It’s

102
00:05:55.109 --> 00:06:01.289
chi, since it’s in constant change.

103
00:06:01.289 --> 00:06:04.629
So in fact, if we want to work on this, we must

104
00:06:04.942 --> 00:06:10.462
embrace impermanence. So to open our vision, we

106
00:06:10.462 --> 00:06:14.562
must be genuinely attentive to every moment,

107
00:06:15.662 --> 00:06:20.722
to each thought, to every detail. This means we must learn to see beyond

108
00:06:20.722 --> 00:06:20.962
our

109
00:06:20.962 --> 00:06:26.682
projections, beyond our fears. This is where we must gradually learn to

110
00:06:26.682 --> 00:06:28.982
free ourselves from our

111
00:06:30.542 --> 00:06:32.682
false interpretations. It’s not easy.

112
00:06:33.014 --> 00:06:36.534
Because sometimes, we even want to remain fixed in our ideology.

113
00:06:37.754 --> 00:06:38.834
So, it's not complicated.

114
00:06:39.654 --> 00:06:42.794
As soon as you think you are in reality, you are mistaken.

115
00:06:46.134 --> 00:06:50.474
What I suggest to you is to increasingly harness your inner strength.

116
00:06:54.494 --> 00:06:58.514
Leverage, readjust your ideas about chance and success.

117
00:06:59.434 --> 00:07:00.854
Have the right intention.

118
00:07:02.287 --> 00:07:07.367
This morning, I expressed something to you. We will work with your

119
00:07:07.367 --> 00:07:08.107
center of gravity,

120
00:07:08.367 --> 00:07:14.207
your whole body, in service of your hands. Vital energy, it

121
00:07:14.207 --> 00:07:15.327
is in the abdomen.

122
00:07:16.547 --> 00:07:22.967
It’s one of the important centers. This impermanence supports

123
00:07:22.967 --> 00:07:23.867
this vital energy.

124
00:07:25.007 --> 00:07:28.067
So if you gradually manage to really adjust yourself,

125
00:07:29.159 --> 00:07:33.759
With your own center, it will be much more powerful, surprisingly.

126
00:07:34.399 --> 00:07:38.799
And you may have felt a bit this morning when I asked you to adjust.

127
00:07:39.539 --> 00:07:43.499
I did it, I asked you to adjust; you just need to adjust.

128
00:07:43.719 --> 00:07:47.439
Because we will work with three major types of energy, three main types of movement.

129
00:07:47.939 --> 00:07:53.199
We will work with induced movement, we will work with permitted movement,

130
00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:56.039
and we will work with present movement.

131
00:07:57.232 --> 00:07:58.952
I can induce something.

132
00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:01.232
I must do it consciously.

133
00:08:02.472 --> 00:08:04.612
Or I can follow something.

134
00:08:06.672 --> 00:08:09.032
Or I can just listen to the present moment.

135
00:08:11.612 --> 00:08:14.792
So it's about accepting your strength, accepting your weakness.

136
00:08:15.012 --> 00:08:17.052
And also understanding the difference between them.

137
00:08:18.092 --> 00:08:23.112
And opening your heart to the countless possibilities that are

138
00:08:23.112 --> 00:08:23.252
there.

139
00:08:23.252 --> 00:08:25.232
Often...

140
00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:27.804
When I have people like that coming in with quite acute problems,

141
00:08:28.584 --> 00:08:33.844
not just minor issues but quite deep ones, depressive states, things like that,

142
00:08:33.844 --> 00:08:34.364
I ask them a question, I say, hey, when you are healed, what will you be able to do? 

143
00:08:41.304 --> 00:08:43.524
What will you be able to do again?

144
00:08:43.964 --> 00:08:47.184
It’s a whole new program that sometimes they hadn’t even thought about.

145
00:08:48.184 --> 00:08:51.064
It’s important because you create a direction.

146
00:08:51.804 --> 00:08:53.304
And that’s what we need to work with health.

147
00:08:53.997 --> 00:08:59.137
We should not work with illness or against illness; we should work

148
00:08:59.137 --> 00:08:59.717
with health.

149
00:09:00.797 --> 00:09:05.937
And so sometimes this path is very narrow, directing our attention towards

150
00:09:05.937 --> 00:09:06.397
health.